      "id": 1,
      "text": "Edmundson began as the Edmundson Terrace subdivision opened for sale on December 3, 1941.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/edmundson_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village incorporated on May 12, 1948, and became a fourth‑class city in 1993.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmundson%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original subdivision spanned roughly 25 acres, contained 156 homes, and housed about 500 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/edmundson_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its boundaries were the same 25‑acre subdivision, bordered by Natural Bridge Road to the north and Edmundson Road to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/edmundson_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early commercial life featured a restaurant, service stations, a confectionary, and Hoyt Archery Company near Natural Bridge Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/edmundson_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town’s name derives from the Edmundson Terrace subdivision that opened in 1941, reflecting post‑World War II suburban growth.",
